From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lasimeri <217267696+Lasimeri@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 09:00:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] x86/knc: tty on the host/card ring

The early console is output only, so init cannot open /dev/console and
nothing typed on the host reaches the card. Add ttyPHI0: output shares
the card-to-host console ring with the early console (now under a lock
in knc_earlycon.c, which also keeps the host-to-card ring once the
permanent mapping is up), input is polled from the host-to-card ring
every 10 ms by a delayed work (ring protocol v1 has no signaling). The
console registers as ttyPHI so console=ttyPHI0 makes it the kernel
console and the boot console is dropped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
